windowClickT -- windows stroke 2 (SEQ 749, 2026-11-22): a click from a point (W2), and selection shown with selectFill (W3).
A delta of tabClickT's preamble (copied, then patched). Rows in genLadder/formsPop.sh, run at GCSTRESS=1000. No window is
shown: windowClick(request) makes a mouse-up event at px, py (counted from the view's top left, as pixelAt counts) and
sends it to the view's own mouseUp, so the road tested is the one a real click takes. After each click the fixture lays
the form out again and hands the window the new copy (windowHold); a live window doing that itself is stroke 3.

WC-0  tabForm laid out, in a window, read: nothing selected, tab One and the card green (tabClickT's TK-0).
WC-1  a point inside tab Three: the window finds tabThree on the copy, clickField selects it and fires its onClick
      (tabClick, selectTab). Redrawn: tab Three and the whole card red, tab One tabFill -- TK-1's page, from a point.
WC-2  a point in the card: the hit is thirdCard, the card shown (the two hidden cards do not catch it). Nothing has an
      action on the way up, and it says so, naming how many fields it tried (thirdCard, bodies, body, tabForm).
WC-3  a point outside the form: no field, nothing fired, said so.

wcForm sits at x=20 y=30, so a hit also proves the form's own origin is added. Its look, wcLook, holds selectFill:=blue.
WS-0  as declared: wcInner red, wcPlain the page's white (it names no fill), wcLower green.
WS-1  a point in wcInner. BUBBLING: wcInner has no action, so its parent wcOuter's onClick fires, handed wcOuter.
      SELECTION: wcInner is drawn blue, the look's selectFill.
WS-2  a point in wcPlain: it has no fill of its own and is given one, blue; wcInner is red again.
WS-3  a point in wcLower, which names its own selectFill:=wall: its own wins over the look's (wall, not blue). Nothing
      fires on the way up (wcLower, wcBody, wcForm).
WS-4  wcPlain selected, then laid out under a request naming no look: the selectFill is defaultLook's, lightBlue (Tony,
      2026-11-22), not wcLook's blue. (Before defaultLook held one this row read white: drawn as it was.)
WS-5  the mock click by name (click) selects wcInner on the definition: it does not climb (no WC-SAY), and the next
      layout under wcLook shows it blue -- selection is matched by name, whichever click made it.
